# Percent armour (server/README.md "Percent armour"): a player's armour reduced a physical hit by a random flat amount
# (stock: uniform(armour / 2, armour - 1)), which blocked small hits completely and hardly mattered against the late-game
# ones. With armorPercent = true (default) a player's armour takes armour / (armour + armorPercentConstant) of a physical
# hit (rounded), at most armorPercentMax % (defaults 250 and 80): 100 armour 28.6%, 150 37.5%, 200 44.4%. Only
# COMBAT_PHYSICALDAMAGE that is blocked by armour (melee, distance weapons, "physical" monster spells, spells with
# COMBAT_PARAM_BLOCKARMOR); elemental damage is not reduced by armour (the stock formula took the flat amount from a
# blockArmor elemental hit too). Defence (the shield block: blockCount, uniform(def / 2, def)) is unchanged and comes
# first, as before. Monsters keep the stock formula (their armour values are tuned for it). armorPercent = false is the
# stock formula for players again. configKeys.ARMOR_PERCENT / ARMOR_PERCENT_CONSTANT / ARMOR_PERCENT_MAX;
# Creature::armorPercentReduction(armour) is the share. Simulation: server/tools/armor_sim.py.
# Apply in the server source root after 0001-0015: patch -p1 < 0016-percent-armour.patch, then rebuild.
